/-!
# Two-generator regular-sequence blowup atlas

Source: Stacks Project, More on Algebra, Tag 0BIQ; Resolution of Surfaces, Tag 0AGQ;
Divisors, Tags 0804 and 02OS; Algebra, Tags 00FN and 00E8
(blueprint: lem-sfb-two-parameter-blowup-atlas).

The affine blowup is the recorded Rees-algebra Proj model. Its chart embeddings are the
existing `AffineBlowup.chartRingι`, obtained from the homogeneous-localization comparison.
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u

set_option autoImplicit false

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- The two standard charts of the blowup of `(x,y)`, with their structural algebra
presentations, coordinates, exceptional equations and Noetherianity.

Source: Stacks Project, Tags 0BIQ, 0AGQ, 0804, 02OS, 00FN and 00E8.
(blueprint: lem-sfb-two-parameter-blowup-atlas)

Here `I` with `hI` is the ideal `(x,y)`. The elements are bundled in `I` only to supply
membership to the existing chart maps. The chart assertion is made for the two ordered
pairs `(x,y)` and `(y,x)`. The inner pullback projection is the closed immersion
`Z = Y ×_[Spec A] Spec (A/I) → Y`; the outer pullback restricts it to each chart.

Proof:
1. Apply prop-nagata-affine-blowup-chart-cover to the two generators. The canonical
   def-nagata-affine-blowup-chart-map and prop-nagata-affine-blowup-chart identify the
   chart ranges with `D_+(xT)` and `D_+(yT)`, over `Spec A`.
2. Apply lem-trf-blowup-chart-regular-sequence-presentation to both orderings, using
   their separate regularity hypotheses. Identify the polynomial ring in one variable
   with the `Fin 1` multivariable ring. The image of the variable is the specified
   ratio, and def-nagata-homogeneous-away-to-chart identifies this with the homogeneous
   coordinate `(bT)/(aT)`.
3. Each presentation is a quotient of a polynomial algebra in one variable. Apply
   lem-weil-pbc-finite-type-algebra-noetherian to obtain Noetherian chart rings.
4. Apply lemma-nagata-chart-extended-ideal-principal and
   lemma-nagata-chart-generator-regular on both charts, transporting along the existing
   homogeneousAwayEquivChart. The extended ideals are generated by the structural
   images of the respective parameters, and multiplication by them is injective.
5. Pullback pasting and lem-weil-pbc-fibre-product-affine-spectra identify the restriction
   of `Z` with `Spec ((A/I) ⊗[A] C)`. Clause (1) of
   lem-weil-pbc-tensor-over-quotient-ring sends `ā ⊗ c` to `ac` modulo the extended
   ideal. This map preserves products and one, hence is a ring isomorphism. It identifies
   the chart projection with Spec of the quotient map of def-weil-pbc-algebra-hom-quotient.
6. The extended ideal is locally generated by the nonzerodivisors in step 4, so the
   open-cover criterion of def-nagata-effective-cartier-ideal makes the kernel of
   the closed immersion `Z → Y` invertible.
7. The two Noetherian affine charts give local Noetherianity by pqf-def-locnoeth.
   Each affine spectrum is quasi-compact by clause (iii) of
   lem-weil-pbc-spec-basic-opens-unit-ideal-quasi-compact. Restrict an arbitrary open
   cover to the two charts and unite their finite subcovers. Thus `Y` is quasi-compact
   as well, exactly the meaning of `IsNoetherian`.
-/
theorem twoParameterBlowupAtlas
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A]
    (I : Ideal A) (x y : I)
    (hI : Ideal.span ({(x : A), (y : A)} : Set A) = I)
    (hxy : RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular A [(x : A), (y : A)])
    (hyx : RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular A [(y : A), (x : A)]) :
    ((AffineBlowup.chartRingι I x.property).opensRange ⊔
        (AffineBlowup.chartRingι I y.property).opensRange = ⊤) ∧
    (∀ a b : I, (a = x ∧ b = y) ∨ (a = y ∧ b = x) →
      (AffineBlowup.chartRingι I a.property).opensRange =
        Proj.basicOpen (reesGrading I) (reesX I a a.property) ∧
      AffineBlowup.chartRingι I a.property ≫ AffineBlowup.toSpec I =
        Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A (AffineBlowup.chartRing I a))) ∧
      (∃ e :
          (Polynomial A ⧸ Ideal.span
            {Polynomial.C (a : A) * Polynomial.X - Polynomial.C (b : A)}) ≃ₐ[A]
              AffineBlowup.chartRing I a,
        ((e (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ Polynomial.X) : AffineBlowup.chartRing I a) :
            Localization.Away (a : A)) = AffineBlowup.chartFraction (a : A) 1 (b : A) ∧
        e (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ Polynomial.X) =
          AffineBlowup.homogeneousAwayToChart I a.property
            (HomogeneousLocalization.Away.mk (reesGrading I)
              (reesX_mem I a a.property) 1 (reesX I b b.property)
              (reesX_mem I b b.property))) ∧
      IsNoetherianRing (AffineBlowup.chartRing I a) ∧
      I.map (algebraMap A (AffineBlowup.chartRing I a)) =
        Ideal.span {algebraMap A (AffineBlowup.chartRing I a) (a : A)} ∧
      Function.Injective (fun c : AffineBlowup.chartRing I a ↦
        algebraMap A (AffineBlowup.chartRing I a) (a : A) * c) ∧
      (∃ eZ :
          pullback (AffineBlowup.chartRingι I a.property)
            (pullback.fst (AffineBlowup.toSpec I)
              (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)))) ≅
          Spec (.of (AffineBlowup.chartRing I a ⧸
            I.map (algebraMap A (AffineBlowup.chartRing I a)))),
        eZ.hom ≫ Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk
            (I.map (algebraMap A (AffineBlowup.chartRing I a))))) =
          pullback.fst (AffineBlowup.chartRingι I a.property)
            (pullback.fst (AffineBlowup.toSpec I)
              (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)))))) ∧
    IsClosedImmersion (pullback.fst (AffineBlowup.toSpec I)
      (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)))) ∧
    (pullback.fst (AffineBlowup.toSpec I)
      (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)))).ker.IsInvertible ∧
    IsNoetherian (AffineBlowup I) := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry
